    "answer": {
      "short": "$(n+1)^2-n^2=2n+1=(n+1)+n$.",
      "worked": "Let the consecutive integers be $n$ and $n+1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}(n+1)^2-n^2&=n^2+2n+1-n^2\\\\&=2n+1\\\\&=(n+1)+n\\end{align*}$$\nThus the square of the larger integer minus the square of the smaller integer equals the sum of the two integers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
